WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.100 --> 00:01.920
Why do I feel like I don't suspect Amp?

3
00:01.920 --> 00:02.950
Get a grip, Podduang.

4
00:02.950 --> 00:04.280
A hater is a hater.

5
00:04.280 --> 00:05.000
[Don't get involved in Anda's case if you still want to live.]

6
00:05.000 --> 00:06.520
Do you think it's Amp?

7
00:06.520 --> 00:08.210
Why would she do something like that?

8
00:08.210 --> 00:10.920
She knows we're investigating this. That's why.

9
00:10.920 --> 00:14.120
Anda said if the day came when he had to go,

10
00:14.120 --> 00:15.590
[If my mom knows that I like my friend,] he wanted you two

11
00:15.590 --> 00:17.663
[will she be happy?] to bring the box to the cremation as well.

12
00:19.130 --> 00:21.850
I'll return and take over your business.

13
00:21.850 --> 00:25.150
You have to let me see every CCTV camera in your condo.

14
00:25.150 --> 00:27.360
Amp, James's girlfriend...

15
00:27.360 --> 00:28.490
Jealousy is clearly the motive.

16
00:28.490 --> 00:30.430
They've fought over this many times.

17
00:30.430 --> 00:33.860
And do you know where James is now?

18
00:33.860 --> 00:35.920
I really do promise.

19
00:35.920 --> 00:37.763
I'll definitely get the money.

20
00:38.350 --> 00:39.716
A million, okay?

21
00:39.716 --> 00:42.160
Boss, he's asking for another million.

22
00:42.160 --> 00:44.703
I've found someone with even worse luck than you.

23
00:51.360 --> 00:52.483
No...

24
00:59.760 --> 01:01.520
Please...

25
01:08.640 --> 01:10.820
Don't do anything to me. I'm begging.

26
01:10.820 --> 01:13.223
No, please!

27
01:22.350 --> 01:24.360
What's next, Boss?

28
01:24.360 --> 01:25.843
You can take a break for now.

29
01:28.490 --> 01:30.330
Let this guy take over.

30
01:31.840 --> 01:32.930
Go on.

31
01:42.624 --> 01:43.830
Go!

32
02:09.040 --> 02:13.200
[Characters, places, and incidents in this production]

33
02:13.200 --> 02:14.880
[are entirely fictitious.]

34
02:14.880 --> 02:16.776
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

35
03:48.430 --> 03:49.923
What's wrong?

36
03:52.200 --> 03:53.730
Nothing, sir.

37
03:57.410 --> 03:58.776
Are you scared?

38
04:01.170 --> 04:03.120
Don't be.

39
04:03.120 --> 04:07.280
That security guard... only asked me for one million.

40
04:07.280 --> 04:09.996
If you can't come up with two million to repay me,

41
04:09.996 --> 04:11.970
you'll get the best treatment.

42
04:11.970 --> 04:14.240
Please don't kill me, sir.

43
04:14.240 --> 04:17.600
- Please don't kill me. - Hey.

44
04:17.600 --> 04:19.750
Why would I kill you?

45
04:19.750 --> 04:22.160
You're so useful.

46
04:22.160 --> 04:24.256
I'll be keeping you around.

47
04:25.520 --> 04:27.550
I'll get you the money as soon as I can.

48
04:28.656 --> 04:31.830
No. You don't need to.

49
04:35.230 --> 04:37.830
Do you want your debt to be wiped out?

50
04:56.040 --> 04:57.856
What do you want me to do, sir?

51
04:59.640 --> 05:02.160
You're quite a quick learner.

52
05:02.160 --> 05:05.880
I'm ready, sir. I'll do anything.

53
05:05.880 --> 05:10.470
I heard you acted with my brother in those shows.

54
05:11.550 --> 05:12.683
Yes, sir.

55
05:13.340 --> 05:15.730
But I didn't realize that your girlfriend...

56
05:20.276 --> 05:22.430
was one of my brother's haters.

57
05:26.880 --> 05:28.269
Well?

58
05:31.370 --> 05:35.910
Now, guess what I want you to do next.

59
05:37.240 --> 05:39.483
Sir... Sir.

60
05:43.450 --> 05:45.616
Hey.

61
05:46.300 --> 05:48.150
There's no need to kill anyone.

62
05:49.613 --> 05:51.623
I'm not that cold-hearted.

63
05:52.550 --> 05:55.400
But do you know your girlfriend...

64
05:55.400 --> 05:58.736
is the prime suspect in my brother's case right now?

65
06:01.310 --> 06:02.680
I know about that, sir.

66
06:02.680 --> 06:05.110
But I really don't know if she killed Anda or not.

67
06:05.110 --> 06:09.360
I swear, I don't know. I haven't contacted her.

68
06:09.360 --> 06:12.270
I don't know where she is, sir.

69
06:12.270 --> 06:14.400
Stop talking.

70
06:14.400 --> 06:16.103
It's annoying.

71
06:23.870 --> 06:27.510
I just want to know where she is.

72
06:27.510 --> 06:29.430
And can you get a hold of her?

73
06:30.210 --> 06:34.160
We've been arguing about money lately.

74
06:34.160 --> 06:36.960
She disappeared. I called, but she didn't answer.

75
06:36.960 --> 06:40.490
Do you have any idea where she might be?

76
06:40.490 --> 06:42.330
I don't know.

77
06:46.173 --> 06:48.460
You're starting to become useless to me.

78
06:48.460 --> 06:51.355
Sir! Sir.

79
06:51.355 --> 06:54.320
I'll find her as soon as I can, sir.

80
06:54.320 --> 06:57.200
I promise I'll find her.

81
06:58.900 --> 07:00.056
Yeah.

82
07:09.640 --> 07:13.930
Bring me your girlfriend, and I'll wipe out your debt.

83
07:15.490 --> 07:16.683
Sir.

84
07:17.480 --> 07:20.563
What are you going to do to her? She's pregnant right now.

85
07:24.880 --> 07:29.290
What could a "good" cop like me do to a pregnant woman?

86
07:33.790 --> 07:35.550
The one who's going to do it...

87
07:36.140 --> 07:38.030
is you.

88
07:52.870 --> 07:53.790
[Who killed Anda?] [Amp's Teddy, Kum, Thieving Security Guard]

89
07:58.120 --> 08:02.400
Are you two Sherlock Holmes? I've got Conan in my room. That's enough.

90
08:02.400 --> 08:04.800
Now I have to deal with Sherlock and Watson, too.

91
08:04.800 --> 08:06.476
I'm totally lost now.

92
08:08.610 --> 08:10.463
What did you two find?

93
08:11.280 --> 08:15.460
We tested the CAN bus system we talked about the other day.

94
08:15.460 --> 08:17.240
Art and I tried it out ourselves.

95
08:17.240 --> 08:20.380
[A modification shop?] The professor tested it on Anda's car model.

96
08:20.380 --> 08:23.160
That model isn't even difficult to hack.

97
08:23.160 --> 08:26.080
So now we can be 100% certain, right?

98
08:26.080 --> 08:28.440
That the car was hacked.

99
08:28.440 --> 08:35.169
Yes. The professor also inspected Anda's car for the police.

100
08:35.169 --> 08:37.145
Which means...

101
08:37.145 --> 08:41.320
The killer didn't have to be at the crime scene, right?

102
08:41.320 --> 08:42.480
Exactly.

103
08:42.480 --> 08:45.240
Are there any range limitations?

104
08:45.240 --> 08:48.040
There are three ranges: Near, mid, and far.

105
08:48.040 --> 08:51.283
Far means unlimited. It can be done remotely.

106
08:51.960 --> 08:54.776
That makes it really hard to identify the culprit.

107
08:56.020 --> 08:58.710
Yeah, we don't have enough information.

108
09:01.570 --> 09:04.996
It's not much, but it's a start.

109
09:07.190 --> 09:11.220
Stop showing off. Just tell us what you know.

110
09:11.220 --> 09:14.290
There are many auto repair shops in Bangkok.

111
09:14.290 --> 09:19.756
But few can install smart systems in luxury cars like Anda's.

112
09:21.370 --> 09:23.440
What are you getting at, Tod?

113
09:23.440 --> 09:26.180
So you'll check the repair shops, right?

114
09:26.180 --> 09:27.575
Yes.

115
09:27.575 --> 09:31.576
Easy. I'll ask Itti where Anda had his car serviced.

116
09:32.640 --> 09:37.270
If the killer had access to the car, Amp probably isn't involved, right?

117
09:37.270 --> 09:38.240
[Amp (Anda's hater)] [James - James's car]

118
09:38.240 --> 09:40.000
[Not a suicide] From what I know,

119
09:40.000 --> 09:44.890
she has no connection to cars except paying for James's.

120
09:44.890 --> 09:48.320
But we can't rule her out yet. Amp is something else.

121
09:48.320 --> 09:50.320
She's a ruthless hater.

122
09:50.320 --> 09:52.890
She could've used her skills to sabotage Anda's car.

123
09:52.890 --> 09:55.640
- Who knows? - You've watched too many movies.

124
09:55.640 --> 09:58.975
Anything's possible right now.

125
09:58.975 --> 10:02.196
We're just students, but look at us now.

126
10:04.260 --> 10:06.530
We've come this far.

127
10:07.540 --> 10:09.176
Let's end this matter.

128
10:12.080 --> 10:13.796
[Who killed Anda?] [Amp's Teddy, Kum, Thieving Security Guard]

129
10:15.390 --> 10:20.080
We don't want to ruin the moment, but weren't we here to drink?

130
10:20.080 --> 10:24.420
We've been staring at this board all day. We're tired too, you know.

131
10:24.420 --> 10:28.760
So Jinna invited you two for drinks?

132
10:28.760 --> 10:30.176
Exactly.

133
10:32.704 --> 10:34.009
Podduang.

134
10:35.160 --> 10:37.400
That means...

135
10:37.400 --> 10:39.443
You tricked us into coming here, too?

136
10:40.290 --> 10:43.320
Come on. We hardly ever get together.

137
10:43.320 --> 10:46.800
If I hadn't done this, the case wouldn't have moved forward.

138
10:46.800 --> 10:50.423
- And we wouldn't have gotten together. - Who said I tricked you?

139
10:59.960 --> 11:01.800
To our friendship!

140
11:01.800 --> 11:04.040
- Cheers! - Cheers!

141
11:04.040 --> 11:06.760
- Bottoms up! - Not me.

142
11:06.760 --> 11:09.383
- Last one to finish has to drink another! - That's me.

143
11:10.780 --> 11:13.543
Hey, guys, we're out of ice.

144
11:16.040 --> 11:20.560
Let's spin the bottle to see who buys more ice.

145
11:20.560 --> 11:22.850
Here, I'll spin it.

146
11:26.870 --> 11:28.700
It's you, Dunk.

147
11:28.700 --> 11:30.360
Come on!

148
11:30.360 --> 11:34.200
Come on! Who's paying this round?

149
11:34.200 --> 11:36.683
I'll do it. Help me, my boy.

150
11:38.300 --> 11:39.376
Watch this.

151
11:43.360 --> 11:44.740
Oops!

152
11:44.740 --> 11:47.040
It's Jinna.

153
11:47.040 --> 11:48.200
That's awesome.

154
11:49.840 --> 11:51.883
Fine, I'll go with Dunk.

155
11:54.880 --> 11:56.740
Hurry back,

156
11:56.740 --> 12:01.200
or Bum and I might have to drink it straight.

157
12:01.200 --> 12:05.770
- You're really something, aren't you? - Look at you two lovebirds.

158
12:05.770 --> 12:08.600
Jinna is so slick.

159
12:08.600 --> 12:12.310
We'll go get it together. Let's go.

160
12:15.480 --> 12:18.730
- Can you still practice tomorrow? - I'm fine.

161
12:18.730 --> 12:21.050
- What's there to worry about? - I'm fine. What about you?

162
12:21.050 --> 12:24.083
Of course! I'm the host.

163
12:24.880 --> 12:27.280
- Is that so? - Yeah.

164
12:27.280 --> 12:29.943
So, are you two actually dating?

165
12:29.943 --> 12:31.680
We've been dating for a long time.

166
12:31.680 --> 12:34.860
I mean, are you seriously dating?

167
12:34.860 --> 12:37.950
Not just pretending for show.

168
12:41.460 --> 12:43.870
- You knew? - Of course.

169
12:43.870 --> 12:46.910
Podduang's my best friend. Of course I know.

170
12:48.540 --> 12:51.770
But did you know... he likes you?

171
12:52.800 --> 12:56.090
He used to, but not anymore.

172
12:56.090 --> 12:58.763
I can tell by the way he looks at you, Jinna.

173
12:59.440 --> 13:00.840
What's with you?

174
13:00.840 --> 13:03.710
- You sound like you want him back. - I wouldn't do that.

175
13:03.710 --> 13:06.356
I'm actually glad he likes you.

176
13:08.360 --> 13:09.583
Why's that?

177
13:10.190 --> 13:13.260
You two are so obvious.

178
13:13.260 --> 13:15.580
You've liked him for ages, haven't you?

179
13:15.580 --> 13:18.790
Take good care of him. And one more thing.

180
13:18.790 --> 13:22.610
If you hurt Podduang, I'll make you pay.

181
13:22.610 --> 13:25.120
- Are you threatening me? - You could call it that.

182
13:25.120 --> 13:27.360
So you'd better be a little scared of me.

183
13:27.360 --> 13:31.076
Bum and I care about Podduang just as much as you do.

184
13:31.076 --> 13:34.930
- Got it? - Yeah, I understand.

185
13:34.930 --> 13:37.408
Come on. The ice is melting at my feet.

186
13:37.408 --> 13:38.470
Go.

187
13:44.216 --> 13:47.800
Give it here. You sound like a dying cat.

188
13:47.800 --> 13:49.770
Let me sing, too.

189
13:49.770 --> 13:52.880
- No way. You're a terrible singer. - No.

190
13:52.880 --> 13:54.463
Yuck.

191
13:59.110 --> 14:01.810
Do you usually drink this much?

192
14:01.810 --> 14:04.556
You saw how much I drank. It was my birthday.

193
14:06.360 --> 14:08.630
Right. That's true.

194
14:08.630 --> 14:10.803
I didn't think you'd get so drunk, though.

195
14:15.632 --> 14:18.870
Here. Have another can.

196
14:18.870 --> 14:20.390
Or do you want two?

197
14:21.240 --> 14:23.010
Aren't you being a little too nice?

198
14:26.750 --> 14:29.810
He's trying to get you drunk, Podduang.

199
14:31.960 --> 14:33.703
Absolutely.

200
14:38.450 --> 14:39.683
Really?

201
14:40.340 --> 14:42.070
No.

202
14:42.070 --> 14:45.440
I just saw that you were happy.

203
14:45.440 --> 14:49.376
We've been through a lot. It's nice to unwind sometimes.

204
14:51.590 --> 14:52.850
Then...

205
14:53.590 --> 14:55.036
Drink with me.

206
14:55.904 --> 14:57.156
Sure thing.

207
15:04.550 --> 15:06.743
At this rate, they'll be at it all night.

208
15:18.960 --> 15:21.716
Wait, Podduang. Take it easy.

209
15:24.250 --> 15:27.070
- Enough talking. - Podduang.

210
15:30.263 --> 15:33.740
Podduang. Someone might hear us.

211
15:33.740 --> 15:35.600
Not yet. The door isn't locked.

212
15:35.600 --> 15:39.000
- They're already asleep. Don't worry. - Podduang, Podduang.

213
15:39.000 --> 15:41.330
Easy. Take it slow, okay?

214
15:41.330 --> 15:44.250
Take it easy. Slow down.

215
15:45.000 --> 15:48.310
- I'm so hot. - Calm down first.

216
15:48.310 --> 15:53.400
- Our friends are outside. - They're asleep. What's there to fear?

217
15:53.400 --> 15:54.716
Podduang.

218
15:58.120 --> 15:59.210
Stop.

219
15:59.890 --> 16:02.810
- I'm hot. - Podduang, please.

220
16:02.810 --> 16:05.180
The others might hear us.

221
16:05.180 --> 16:08.600
- Can you take my shirt off? - Podduang.

222
16:08.600 --> 16:11.660
- Take my shirt off. - You're too drunk.

223
16:11.660 --> 16:13.223
Podduang, Podduang, Podduang.

224
16:15.370 --> 16:17.456
You're so drunk.

225
17:04.110 --> 17:06.116
Jinna, I can't wait any longer.

226
19:20.720 --> 19:23.343
What is this?

227
19:34.910 --> 19:36.560
Hello, Bum.

228
19:36.560 --> 19:38.260
Hello.

229
19:38.260 --> 19:40.500
Where are you, Bum?

230
19:40.500 --> 19:42.143
In my room.

231
19:42.802 --> 19:45.800
When did you guys leave? You didn't even say goodbye.

232
19:45.800 --> 19:48.000
You don't remember anything, do you?

233
19:48.650 --> 19:50.956
That's it. I'm going back to sleep.

234
19:50.956 --> 19:53.523
Wait, what?

235
20:02.790 --> 20:04.870
How did they even get in?

236
20:10.790 --> 20:12.610
Jinna.

237
20:12.610 --> 20:14.970
Let's shower together. Take my shirt off.

238
20:14.970 --> 20:16.370
Podduang, Podduang.

239
20:16.370 --> 20:20.043
Take my shirt off. Can you take my shirt off?

240
20:23.960 --> 20:26.600
Jinna, my friend's quite the flirt, isn't he?

241
20:26.600 --> 20:28.640
It's hot. So hot.

242
20:28.640 --> 20:32.710
I think I'd better head back. I forgot to do laundry. See you.

243
20:32.710 --> 20:34.600
- Yeah, right. - Jinna.

244
20:34.600 --> 20:36.456
Wait for me!

245
20:40.050 --> 20:42.170
Come on. Let's head back.

246
20:42.810 --> 20:44.496
Let's go. Back to our room.

247
20:51.010 --> 20:53.536
- Let's shower together. - Hey.

248
20:59.840 --> 21:02.776
What on earth have I done?

249
21:19.840 --> 21:21.783
How many rounds last night?

250
21:24.360 --> 21:27.236
What messy eaters.

251
21:32.100 --> 21:33.410
Have a seat.

252
21:34.010 --> 21:35.490
I'll give you a ride home.

253
21:36.910 --> 21:39.080
It's okay. I can get home on my own.

254
21:39.080 --> 21:41.670
Hey, it's fine.

255
21:42.430 --> 21:43.863
I can give you a ride.

256
21:44.780 --> 21:48.460
It's surprising that tycoon Chanin,

257
21:48.460 --> 21:52.720
the owner of a leading real estate firm, is stepping down,

258
21:52.720 --> 21:57.056
and his son from his second marriage will take over.

259
22:00.100 --> 22:03.090
You and your dad made up, right?

260
22:04.120 --> 22:05.640
Yeah.

261
22:05.640 --> 22:07.152
Even though I didn't want to.

262
22:07.152 --> 22:09.396
Why is that?

263
22:11.730 --> 22:14.144
I agreed to reconcile with him on two conditions:

264
22:16.160 --> 22:18.489
First, that he'd let me see all the CCTV footage...

265
22:19.500 --> 22:21.496
And second, that he'd make sure you're safe.

266
22:24.067 --> 22:25.223
What?

267
22:29.490 --> 22:31.543
Ever since the incident with Anda,

268
22:32.150 --> 22:34.443
your life has been in danger.

269
22:35.240 --> 22:37.503
I don't want anything to happen to you.

270
22:39.720 --> 22:41.210
Thanks.

271
22:42.770 --> 22:46.390
But why did you mention me to your dad?

272
23:12.890 --> 23:17.450
My dad offered me a car, but I think this is better.

273
23:17.450 --> 23:19.270
What do you mean?

274
23:21.760 --> 23:25.383
Isn't it better to stay close like this?

275
23:26.840 --> 23:27.983
Hey.

276
23:30.930 --> 23:33.076
But don't you think this is a bit much?

277
23:35.780 --> 23:37.930
I understand.

278
23:37.930 --> 23:42.330
That threat you received really worries me.

279
23:45.310 --> 23:46.890
Are you worried about me?

280
23:47.680 --> 23:48.929
Yeah.

281
23:50.647 --> 23:51.876
And...

282
23:53.770 --> 23:56.136
Do they really have to follow us this closely?

283
23:57.020 --> 23:59.710
I don't want to make you uncomfortable.

284
23:59.710 --> 24:03.840
They'll just drive you when I'm not around.

285
24:03.840 --> 24:05.570
And...

286
24:05.570 --> 24:08.456
keep an eye on you whenever you're outside the condo. That's all.

287
24:10.250 --> 24:11.689
That's all?

288
24:38.240 --> 24:39.523
What are you doing?

289
24:41.540 --> 24:42.996
What?

290
24:44.310 --> 24:45.843
What's that mark on your neck?

291
24:48.360 --> 24:49.800
It's just a scratch.

292
24:52.400 --> 24:54.836
What kind of scratch is that?

293
24:55.480 --> 24:58.536
- Just focus on your game. - I'm watching YouTube.

294
24:59.780 --> 25:01.603
Fine. Keep watching, then.

295
25:07.540 --> 25:10.450
- When can we go to the beach again? - Right?

296
25:10.450 --> 25:14.183
- But this time, I don't want to go in summer. - How about the "lovely season"?

297
25:24.110 --> 25:25.610
Heading back together?

298
25:27.920 --> 25:32.150
Look at you, shrinking away. Like you're only three cm tall, buddy.

299
25:32.150 --> 25:34.430
Yeah, look at you. Getting all shy?

300
25:36.949 --> 25:38.630
What are you laughing at?

301
25:39.250 --> 25:41.370
I didn't.

302
25:42.430 --> 25:44.030
Stop laughing.

303
25:44.030 --> 25:47.070
- Who laughed? - But you were just laughing.

304
25:47.070 --> 25:49.030
I wasn't, baby.

305
25:49.990 --> 25:51.423
What's with the "baby"?

306
25:52.310 --> 25:53.810
"I wasn't, baby."

307
25:53.810 --> 25:57.650
And this one. His voice doesn't usually sound like that.

308
25:57.650 --> 26:00.530
Now my friend's voice is all sweet and high-pitched.

309
26:00.530 --> 26:03.430
I'm sick of all this lovey-dovey stuff.

310
26:03.430 --> 26:05.510
When are you two making it official?

311
26:08.580 --> 26:10.076
Fine, how about now?

312
26:19.250 --> 26:21.123
The two of us...

313
26:24.210 --> 26:25.630
are dating.

314
26:29.400 --> 26:30.930
Are we?

315
26:32.960 --> 26:35.260
- Quick, answer! - Yeah, we are.

316
26:35.260 --> 26:36.480
Hey!

317
26:36.480 --> 26:40.430
What did he say, Tod? I couldn't quite hear him.

318
26:40.430 --> 26:41.910
- Quick, answer! - I don't know.

319
26:41.910 --> 26:42.900
What did he say?

320
26:42.900 --> 26:45.350
- Mumbling. - Come on, what was it?

321
26:45.350 --> 26:46.770
- Come on, say it. - Hurry up!

322
26:46.770 --> 26:48.070
- What should I say? - Say it!

323
26:48.070 --> 26:51.110
- Say it! Say it! Come on! - Tell us!

324
26:52.295 --> 26:53.500
Come on. Let's hear it.

325
26:53.500 --> 26:55.870
- Hurry! - Podduang, say it!

326
26:55.870 --> 26:57.423
I'm waiting to hear it. Hurry!

327
26:59.410 --> 27:00.523
All right!

328
27:01.430 --> 27:03.170
Jinna and I are dating!

329
27:04.970 --> 27:06.010
Is that clear enough?

330
27:06.010 --> 27:07.960
- I see. - I see.

331
27:07.960 --> 27:10.550
- Crystal clear! - Loud and clear!

332
27:16.650 --> 27:19.850
- Hey, everyone. - Did you hear that?

333
27:19.850 --> 27:23.440
- Loud and clear! - We heard you!

334
27:23.440 --> 27:25.670
- I can't stay here any longer. - Where are you going?

335
27:25.670 --> 27:27.360
Grab him.

336
27:27.360 --> 27:30.910
- That's it. Hold him tight. - Go ahead.

337
27:30.910 --> 27:32.040
- My bag! - He's blushing.

338
27:32.040 --> 27:33.500
What?

339
27:33.500 --> 27:34.890
- I'm heading home. - Give me the bag.

340
27:34.890 --> 27:37.230
Okay, baby.

341
27:37.230 --> 27:38.280
- Yes, baby. - Bye-bye.

342
27:38.280 --> 27:40.450
- Bye-bye. - See you, baby.

343
27:47.280 --> 27:51.283
[Jinna: I'm checking more CCTV footage at Dad's condo today.]

344
27:54.600 --> 27:56.826
[Podduang: Okay. Stop by when you're done.]

345
28:31.980 --> 28:33.563
Can I come in?

346
28:36.700 --> 28:37.850
Yes.

347
28:54.800 --> 28:56.080
Thank you.

348
29:05.450 --> 29:06.896
So...

349
29:08.380 --> 29:11.076
You really didn't kill Anda, did you?

350
29:13.480 --> 29:15.690
Why would I do that?

351
29:18.970 --> 29:20.110
And...

352
29:20.730 --> 29:22.836
Why did you run away?

353
29:26.720 --> 29:28.450
I came here...

354
29:29.350 --> 29:32.770
to tell you the whole truth.

355
29:32.770 --> 29:36.543
If you haven't done anything wrong, why are you so afraid?

356
29:42.940 --> 29:46.163
Because I know if I'd stayed...

357
29:46.870 --> 29:48.663
I'd be dead by now.

358
29:52.010 --> 29:53.810
What do you mean?

359
29:57.540 --> 29:59.610
Then promise me.

360
30:01.470 --> 30:03.503
Don't tell anyone about this.

361
30:04.170 --> 30:06.883
And I'll stay out of this matter from now on.

362
30:09.750 --> 30:10.923
Then...

363
30:11.860 --> 30:13.716
Let me ask you one more thing.

364
30:17.340 --> 30:19.796
Were you the one who sent me that threatening message?

365
30:22.780 --> 30:24.296
What message?

366
30:27.580 --> 30:29.933
[Don't get involved in Anda's case if you still want to live.]

367
30:32.440 --> 30:34.336
It's a death threat.

368
30:36.240 --> 30:39.530
Tycoon Chanin's son, Jinna Ronnarak,

369
30:39.530 --> 30:42.800
currently an undergraduate student,

370
30:42.800 --> 30:47.140
- Is Jinna's dad really this rich? - has officially taken over the business...

371
30:47.140 --> 30:49.440
- Why? - An official press conference was held.

372
30:49.440 --> 30:51.850
Do you want your parents to show up and say...

373
30:51.850 --> 30:54.990
"Actually, our family is worth millions, son"?

374
30:54.990 --> 30:57.000
Well, wouldn't that be great?

375
30:57.000 --> 30:59.590
Then I could take care of you without worrying.

376
30:59.590 --> 31:01.223
Look who's talking.

377
31:05.370 --> 31:07.060
Dunk.

378
31:07.060 --> 31:10.976
Do rich people change cars often?

379
31:13.000 --> 31:17.000
Doesn't that depend on how rich they are?

380
31:17.000 --> 31:19.370
James changes cars very often.

381
31:19.370 --> 31:21.120
But he hasn't changed cars lately.

382
31:21.120 --> 31:24.640
Did he sell them all to get by? He's unemployed and a jerk.

383
31:24.640 --> 31:27.503
Yeah. He's a gambling addict, too.

384
31:28.910 --> 31:31.076
Wait, how do you know that?

385
31:31.850 --> 31:33.860
Just look at him. You don't even need to dig deep.

386
31:33.860 --> 31:38.816
People who flaunt their wealth usually gamble online or play slots.

387
31:42.270 --> 31:46.330
[Audio, AC, Window Tint, Anti-theft, Car Accessories]

388
31:46.330 --> 31:48.740
I'm sure this is the place.

389
31:48.740 --> 31:51.476
I think so, too. This is the last place to check.

390
32:00.528 --> 32:01.590
Hello?

391
32:01.590 --> 32:04.050
Hello, Jinna. What are you doing?

392
32:04.050 --> 32:06.270
I'm checking the CCTV footage. What's up?

393
32:06.270 --> 32:09.540
I found the garage where Anda had his car serviced.

394
32:09.540 --> 32:10.750
But it's weird.

395
32:10.750 --> 32:14.030
Does Itti really not know that Anda brought his car here?

396
32:14.030 --> 32:16.170
His relative owns the place.

397
32:16.170 --> 32:18.700
I don't know. That's what he told me.

398
32:18.700 --> 32:22.550
Yeah, yeah. I'll go talk to them first.

399
32:22.550 --> 32:24.243
Okay.

400
32:28.180 --> 32:30.110
What's next?

401
32:30.110 --> 32:31.660
Let's go. What are we waiting for?

402
32:31.660 --> 32:33.050
Mr. Jinna.

403
32:33.050 --> 32:36.380
I found something in the footage.

404
32:36.380 --> 32:38.130
What is it?

405
32:38.130 --> 32:43.420
The guard who stole the items was seen meeting this person.

406
32:43.420 --> 32:45.743
That's one of Itti's men.

407
32:48.260 --> 32:50.990
- Could you zoom in on that? - Yes, I can.

408
32:57.390 --> 33:00.509
How generous of him. He's even handing out money.

409
33:13.060 --> 33:14.660
I admit it.

410
33:14.660 --> 33:17.280
I used to hate Anda.

411
33:17.280 --> 33:19.743
I hated Anda so much back then that...

412
33:20.620 --> 33:22.743
I couldn't see things clearly.

413
33:23.850 --> 33:27.290
I followed Anda's every move until I knew everything about him.

414
33:27.290 --> 33:31.583
I found out that Anda was actually a really sweet guy.

415
33:34.080 --> 33:36.103
Unlike his brother, though.

416
33:39.190 --> 33:41.270
You mean...

417
33:41.270 --> 33:42.810
Itti?

418
33:42.810 --> 33:44.400
He's the one.

419
33:44.400 --> 33:47.150
The person I believe killed Anda.

420
33:52.330 --> 33:53.730
Hello.

421
33:53.730 --> 33:56.336
How can I help you?

422
33:57.800 --> 34:02.120
We're looking into Anda's case together.

423
34:02.120 --> 34:04.950
You know him, right?

424
34:04.950 --> 34:10.050
Anda was a close friend of ours.

425
34:10.050 --> 34:13.180
But after Anda passed away,

426
34:13.180 --> 34:17.416
we found reason to believe he was murdered.

427
34:21.960 --> 34:27.650
Could you tell us when Anda brought his car in?

428
34:27.650 --> 34:29.043
No, you can't.

429
34:31.320 --> 34:32.830
Listen, sir.

430
34:32.830 --> 34:35.310
We don't need any details, but...

431
34:35.310 --> 34:39.090
- Could we see the CCTV footage-- - It's an invasion of privacy.

432
34:39.090 --> 34:43.040
But if they never find out,

433
34:43.040 --> 34:45.370
it's not an invasion of privacy, right?

434
34:45.370 --> 34:47.003
Come on.

435
34:55.870 --> 34:57.930
All right, what about this?

436
34:57.930 --> 34:59.236
A thousand baht.

437
35:02.672 --> 35:04.510
How about two thousand?

438
35:04.510 --> 35:05.896
Art!

439
35:07.750 --> 35:09.350
Then...

440
35:09.350 --> 35:12.256
Three thousand. Take it or leave it.

441
35:18.210 --> 35:20.796
Anek, come to the counter, please.

442
35:27.363 --> 35:30.560
Enough. I don't have time for this.

443
35:30.560 --> 35:35.270
Get these two out of here. If they come back, deal with them.

444
35:37.680 --> 35:42.263
You heard him. Don't cause any more trouble. Get out!

445
35:43.310 --> 35:45.790
Don't ever come back here.

446
35:48.960 --> 35:50.316
Are you all right?

447
35:51.130 --> 35:54.163
So, how was that? Trying to solve everything with money?

448
35:55.880 --> 35:57.540
Darn.

449
35:57.540 --> 35:59.263
I really thought he'd accept it.

450
36:05.080 --> 36:06.560
Yes, Mr. Jinna.

451
36:06.560 --> 36:10.190
Podduang isn't answering my calls. Could you check on him?

452
36:10.190 --> 36:11.615
Will do.

453
36:11.615 --> 36:13.768
Keep me posted on what happens.

454
36:15.130 --> 36:16.770
Why...

455
36:16.770 --> 36:20.110
You think Itti killed his brother?

456
36:24.563 --> 36:26.809
I think I've found out too much.

457
36:31.230 --> 36:33.640
- I went to a gambling den with James. - The smell of money sure is sweet.

458
36:33.640 --> 36:35.730
James was pretty famous back then.

459
36:35.730 --> 36:37.710
What are we doing here?

460
36:38.710 --> 36:42.190
I'm getting you some spending money. Hey, you don't have to cling to me.

461
36:45.450 --> 36:47.496
Itti was there as well.

462
36:48.830 --> 36:52.030
There he is. He's here.

463
36:53.055 --> 36:55.090
Greet him.

464
36:55.090 --> 36:56.440
- What's up, James? - Hello.

465
36:56.440 --> 36:57.910
Hello.

466
36:57.910 --> 37:00.650
- Ready to get rich today? - Ready as always.

467
37:00.650 --> 37:02.103
Go on, go for it.

468
37:03.320 --> 37:07.232
- I've been on a winning streak lately. - Go. Quickly.

469
37:07.232 --> 37:09.770
- How much will you bet? - Please, come in.

470
37:09.770 --> 37:11.080
What's the limit?

471
37:11.080 --> 37:12.360
- This was also where - No limit.

472
37:12.360 --> 37:13.856
- he liked to trade cars. - Hello, boss.

473
37:14.620 --> 37:17.816
It also seemed to be involved in other illegal activities.

474
37:19.190 --> 37:22.780
Thank you for every bit of support that was sent to both of us.

475
37:22.780 --> 37:25.981
You've acted in three series now. When will you become a real couple?

476
37:25.981 --> 37:28.800
When James started appearing in series with Anda,

477
37:28.800 --> 37:31.528
- he became famous and made more money. - When should it be?

478
37:31.528 --> 37:33.916
That's when James started to change.

479
37:34.520 --> 37:38.376
That's when I started to hate Anda even more.

480
37:38.376 --> 37:42.403
So I created a hate account to attack him.

481
37:43.480 --> 37:47.180
I started digging up dirt on Anda's family to post online...

482
37:47.180 --> 37:52.430
until I found out that Itti actually owned the gambling den

483
37:52.430 --> 37:53.990
and ran those illegal businesses.

484
37:53.990 --> 37:54.630
[Pol. Lt. Col. Itti Thamprateep]

485
37:54.630 --> 37:56.630
[Has Officially Assumed the Position.] The more money James made,

486
37:56.630 --> 38:00.243
the deeper he fell into debt at Itti's gambling den.

487
38:02.250 --> 38:07.009
Stop picking on Anda. You know he's our cash cow.

488
38:08.910 --> 38:11.330
I know you like him.

489
38:13.596 --> 38:17.308
Like him? What's wrong with you? Are you crazy?

490
38:17.950 --> 38:21.150
If I don't do it, we won't get paid.

491
38:21.150 --> 38:24.760
Do you have any money? Then give me 500,000.

492
38:24.760 --> 38:27.950
Haven't I been supporting you all this time?

493
38:27.950 --> 38:29.849
You're so annoying.

494
38:54.320 --> 38:55.800
I know everything.

495
38:57.640 --> 38:59.423
You should leave him.

496
39:02.730 --> 39:06.240
That day changed how I saw Anda.

497
39:06.240 --> 39:09.850
So I decided to tell him the truth about his brother.

498
39:11.280 --> 39:13.856
Are you okay? Can you get up?

499
39:14.600 --> 39:15.770
Take it slow.

500
39:23.040 --> 39:27.030
And all the evidence I had against Itti...

501
39:28.540 --> 39:30.536
I gave it all to Anda.

502
39:33.130 --> 39:34.783
That evidence...

503
39:36.040 --> 39:37.480
What was the evidence?

504
39:41.180 --> 39:43.290
[Installation and Maintenance Anti-theft Alarms, Windows, Central Locks]

505
39:43.290 --> 39:46.696
Darn. What a waste of time.

506
39:48.660 --> 39:54.190
Why do we have to sit by the road like stray dogs?

507
39:59.810 --> 40:04.603
Do you think we'll ever find Anda's killer?

508
40:06.230 --> 40:08.423
Everyone's doing their best.

509
40:08.423 --> 40:10.176
I'm sure we'll find them.

510
40:12.280 --> 40:13.503
Yeah.

511
40:14.530 --> 40:16.670
I feel really sorry for Anda.

512
40:40.605 --> 40:42.676
[Castrol Oil Change Service Center]

513
40:43.424 --> 40:44.516
Hey.

514
40:47.530 --> 40:49.690
Are you thinking what I'm thinking?

515
40:49.690 --> 40:51.396
I'm thinking exactly what you're thinking.

516
41:08.140 --> 41:09.663
What are you guys doing?

517
41:10.390 --> 41:11.710
Investigating something?

518
41:13.320 --> 41:17.115
Hey! You already got a thousand. Stop talking.

519
41:17.115 --> 41:20.183
Tell me. I want to know.

520
41:21.230 --> 41:22.776
A murderer?

521
41:36.280 --> 41:37.800
Hey, Tod. There he is.

522
41:50.840 --> 41:52.550
Shoot.

523
41:52.550 --> 41:54.036
Itti?

524
41:55.120 --> 41:56.896
Shoot, it's Itti.

525
41:58.790 --> 42:00.536
By the way...

526
42:01.540 --> 42:04.840
- Who is this Itti anyway? - Just get lost.

527
42:09.270 --> 42:11.956
- Is anyone here? - Yes?

528
42:12.990 --> 42:14.470
It's you.

529
42:14.470 --> 42:15.943
Is your dad here?

530
42:17.010 --> 42:21.080
- No. He hasn't been home in two days. - Do you know where he went?

531
42:21.080 --> 42:23.160
I don't know.

532
42:23.160 --> 42:24.400
Let me ask you something.

533
42:24.400 --> 42:27.040
When your dad stole those things,

534
42:27.040 --> 42:29.110
did he talk to anyone else?

535
42:30.280 --> 42:32.176
Just you guys.

536
42:34.800 --> 42:38.690
I overheard him on the phone the other day.

537
42:38.690 --> 42:42.483
- It sounded like he was asking for money... - Did you hear anything else?

538
42:43.090 --> 42:46.830
I heard him mention using secrets to expose someone.

539
42:46.830 --> 42:50.750
Something about a phone and a laptop.

540
42:54.260 --> 42:56.030
Did he mention any names?

541
42:57.070 --> 42:59.070
And do you know...

542
42:59.070 --> 43:03.030
that Itti once threatened to kill James over money he owed?

543
43:03.030 --> 43:05.530
Itti is just that terrible.

544
43:12.790 --> 43:14.130
[James: Where are you? Let's meet up. I'm worried.]

545
43:14.130 --> 43:15.440
[I've paid off all my debts. Let's run away.]

546
43:15.440 --> 43:16.416
[Let's start a new life together.]

547
43:21.450 --> 43:23.070
Is something wrong?

548
43:24.310 --> 43:26.330
Nothing.

549
43:26.330 --> 43:28.216
I think I...

550
43:28.960 --> 43:30.556
I should go now.

551
43:31.460 --> 43:34.570
You take care of yourself, too.

552
43:35.720 --> 43:36.750
Okay.

553
43:41.910 --> 43:44.996
I hope what I've told you helps you and your friends.

554
43:58.200 --> 43:59.756
Amp.

555
44:02.280 --> 44:04.510
Please use the back exit.

556
44:04.510 --> 44:06.563
It's dangerous out front.

557
44:51.160 --> 44:52.416
Jinna.

558
44:54.460 --> 44:55.823
Podduang.

559
44:59.010 --> 45:00.256
Jinna.

560
45:02.420 --> 45:03.836
Podduang.

561
45:06.070 --> 45:08.610
Jinna, go help Podduang!

562
45:09.600 --> 45:11.290
Go help Podduang!

563
45:29.940 --> 45:31.990
How are you doing?

564
45:31.990 --> 45:35.623
I was scared, so I didn't dare go out.

565
45:38.130 --> 45:41.856
Then why did you come out so easily?

566
45:49.200 --> 45:50.700
But...

567
45:50.700 --> 45:51.700
You...

568
45:55.200 --> 45:57.790
Hey! What are you doing?

569
46:04.470 --> 46:08.343
You guys really have a death wish.

570
46:19.320 --> 46:21.363
I see almost everyone's here.

571
46:22.210 --> 46:23.570
Who's still missing?

572
46:26.770 --> 46:28.383
Jinna, right?

573
46:29.950 --> 46:32.600
Jinna. Go help Podduang.

574
46:32.600 --> 46:36.130
Jinna, go. Go help Podduang!

575
46:36.130 --> 46:38.050
How could you do this, Itti?

576
46:40.560 --> 46:45.910
Now, tell me which of these three has the least connection to the others.

577
46:45.910 --> 46:47.556
I don't know this guy.

578
46:48.750 --> 46:51.936
As for Amp, I'm done with her.

579
46:55.040 --> 46:56.780
Good.

580
46:56.780 --> 46:58.763
Then your job is done.

581
47:00.350 --> 47:01.869
As promised,

582
47:02.610 --> 47:04.416
your debt is paid off.

583
47:05.860 --> 47:07.256
Which means...

584
47:10.820 --> 47:12.570
You're no use to me anymore.

585
47:32.330 --> 47:34.430
So, who's next?

586
47:42.070 --> 47:44.600
What do you want? Just say it!

587
47:44.600 --> 47:47.230
I want everything you've got on me.

588
47:47.230 --> 47:50.130
Why would I want to keep your dirty little secrets?

589
47:50.130 --> 47:51.230
What are you looking for, Mr. Jinna?

590
47:51.230 --> 47:54.140
Anything that stores data.

591
47:54.140 --> 47:56.440
This isn't how Dad raised you to be.

592
47:56.440 --> 47:59.430
This is all your fault.

593
47:59.430 --> 48:00.710
You did this.

594
48:00.710 --> 48:01.880
You and only you.

595
48:01.880 --> 48:04.640
I think Itti might have abducted Podduang.

596
48:04.640 --> 48:07.610
Killing more people won't make your life any better.

597
48:07.610 --> 48:09.970
I'm not the one who's going to die tonight.

598
48:09.970 --> 48:12.036
You are.
